From: K8s builder bot <k8s-bot@canonical.com>
Subject: [PATCH] recover local storage before strict kubelet startup

Remove only managed local rawfile CSI node sandboxes through CRI before
kubelet resumes after refresh. Retained CSI sandboxes otherwise keep the
old snap mount namespace and cannot propagate new volume mounts to kubelet.
Keep application sandboxes and volume data intact. Fail on runtime errors
so the service wrapper can retain its recovery marker and retry safely.

Use local runtime access for both control-plane and worker nodes, without
Kubernetes administrator credentials. Add the matching Kubernetes CRI API
module and regression tests for scope, partial failure and cancellation.
